                <pb facs="1053" n="957" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg957"/>

                <head>No. 641.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Sickles to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-11-21"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 21,
                        1873</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Constant efforts are made by this cabinet to conciliate England. Castelar is
                    every day at the British legation. The press has received an official hint to
                    contrast the moderation of England with our impatience. I suspect overtures have
                    been made also to Germany for her good offices.</p>
                <closer><signed>SICKLES.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
